1
00:00:17,770 --> 00:00:19,200
How much longer until we arrive?

2
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,500
Less than half a day's ride.

3
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,030
Go inform Chen Lunda.

4
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:24,830
Tell him to come see me shortly.

5
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:25,670
Yes.

6
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,430
I once snuck off to play near Yanmen Pass.

7
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:38,670
My Ata insisted

8
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:40,070
I was a rabbit born in the wrong body,

9
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:41,370
and said he would roast me.

10
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:43,400
Your Ata was wrong.

11
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:45,200
To me, you don't look like a rabbit.

12
00:00:45,370 --> 00:00:46,370
More like a wolf.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,800
Hyah!

14
00:00:56,670 --> 00:00:58,470
Where were we just now?

15
00:00:58,930 --> 00:00:59,730
Yanmen Pass.

16
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,000
Right.

17
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:03,930
Have you been to the border market at Yanmen Pass?

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:04,769
No.

19
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,530
Weisu soldiers may not cross Yanmen Pass.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,030
That was the rule set by Marquis Dingyuan.

21
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:12,600
How would they know you are a warrior of Weisu?

22
00:01:12,870 --> 00:01:14,630
You need a pass to enter the market.

23
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:19,200
The surname Helian stands out too much.

24
00:01:24,930 --> 00:01:27,130
Helian is a noble surname in Weisu.

25
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:29,200
Whose child are you?

26
00:01:29,570 --> 00:01:31,400
It was a name granted to me by the Khan.

27
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,130
My original name is Gerile.

28
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:35,170
My father's name was Bilige.

29
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,670
Your Highness knows my Ata?

30
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:43,800
We knew each other in our youth.

31
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:45,570
He was a hero.

32
00:01:46,470 --> 00:01:47,700
How is he now?

33
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:49,630
He passed away.

34
00:01:53,830 --> 00:01:54,800
Passed away...

35
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:57,229
What is wrong, Your Highness?

36
00:01:58,900 --> 00:01:59,600
Nothing.

37
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:00,800
By the way,

38
00:02:01,130 --> 00:02:02,500
at the banquet duel that night,

39
00:02:02,770 --> 00:02:04,430
Mingke was under imperial orders.

40
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,230
He had no choice but to win.

41
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:06,430
Please do not blame him.

42
00:02:07,130 --> 00:02:08,229
Your Highness is too kind.

43
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:10,070
Lord Chu is an exceptional fighter,

44
00:02:10,229 --> 00:02:11,270
wise and resourceful.

45
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:14,030
To duel with him was a great honor.

46
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:16,230
How could I hold any resentment?

47
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:17,900
To hear you say that

48
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:18,770
puts me at ease.

49
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,030
You are a son of the grasslands.

50
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:22,770
I like you very much.

51
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:25,030
In the days to come, when you two spend time together,

52
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,329
if you can let bygones be bygones,

53
00:02:26,329 --> 00:02:27,570
nothing would please me more.

54
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,070
Lord Chu and I hit it off at first sight.

55
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,470
We are sure to become lifelong friends.

56
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:47,670
Chief, we have arrived.

57
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,600
Make camp.

58
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,170
Make camp!

59
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:03,030
Make camp!

60
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,100
You again.

61
00:03:24,230 --> 00:03:25,800
Where might you be going, my lord?

62
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,770
None of your business.

63
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:34,970
How heartless.

64
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:38,970
Her Highness wants me to befriend you, my lord.

65
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,570
How could it have nothing to do with me?

66
00:03:40,870 --> 00:03:42,030
Helian Zhao.

67
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:43,730
My lord.

68
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:45,000
I am right here.

69
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:49,170
If you dare speak such wanton nonsense again,

70
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:52,370
I will make sure you can never do that again.

71
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,100
Fine, fine.

72
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,000
I will do as you say.

73
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:02,400
You are one of Her Highness's kin.

74
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,070
You guessed wrong, my lord.

75
00:04:04,730 --> 00:04:06,470
I am not her family.

76
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:08,970
I merely happened to receive the Khan's favor.

77
00:04:10,570 --> 00:04:12,330
As long as Her Highness likes you,

78
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:15,170
then you are family to Her Highness.

79
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:22,670
The Plum Garden and the Chen residence,

80
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,770
I will pretend I never saw you there.

81
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:26,100
Just keep your tail well hidden from now on.

82
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:27,700
Then I thank you, my lord.

83
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:39,700
Why don't you guess what they are saying?

84
00:04:40,370 --> 00:04:41,970
Nothing good comes from a dog's mouth.

85
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,930
Whatever it is, it will not be kind.

86
00:04:45,470 --> 00:04:46,900
How broad-minded you are, my lord.

87
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,630
What a pity.

88
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:51,530
Yet with me, you have no patience at all.

89
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,870
Because you are different from others.

90
00:05:14,170 --> 00:05:15,970
I rule this nation with benevolence,

91
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:17,670
valuing both civil and martial virtue.

92
00:05:18,170 --> 00:05:19,530
All under heaven is at peace,

93
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:21,100
and the people live without worry.

94
00:05:21,130 --> 00:05:23,370
Your Majesty's virtue is boundless.

95
00:05:23,470 --> 00:05:24,830
A gentleman does not contend.

96
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:26,230
If he must, let it be in archery.

97
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:28,570
Today, gathered here with my beloved ministers,

98
00:05:28,570 --> 00:05:30,270
let us watch the young men take the field.

99
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,730
By Your Majesty's grace.

100
00:05:31,730 --> 00:05:32,470
Rise.

101
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:33,570
Thank you, Your Majesty.

102
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:36,500
Your Majesty, everything is ready.

103
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:41,570
We may begin.

104
00:05:41,770 --> 00:05:42,330
Yes.

105
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:45,670
Let the willow-shooting contest begin!

106
00:05:52,570 --> 00:05:55,100
Gentlemen, please choose your steeds.

107
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,070
Azhao, choose a horse.

108
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:02,370
You pick first.

109
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:05,170
Let us see if your eye is still as sharp as ever.

110
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,030
Get out of the way, barbarian!

111
00:06:08,030 --> 00:06:08,830
Wusu!

112
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:38,870
Give the command.

113
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:39,630
Yes.

114
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,400
One!

115
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:02,830
Your Majesty.

116
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:03,330
Here it comes.

117
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:04,300
Sit.

118
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:08,300
Your Majesty, cool yourself.

119
00:07:09,670 --> 00:07:11,600
Your Majesty, forgive my lateness.

120
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:14,200
No matter. Sit, my beloved.

121
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:47,500
Hyah!

122
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:02,070
Quick reflexes.

123
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,770
The sun is nearing the western hills.

124
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,700
It is about time, Mingke.

125
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,100
Your Majesty.

126
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,770
Whose pigeon is flying the highest?

127
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,400
Chief, could it be my brother Huabo?

128
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:37,000
Your Majesty, it is Helian Zhao.

129
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,600
Young General Helian,

130
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,570
your aim is superb.

131
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:49,600
Every arrow hits its mark.

132
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,000
The credit is not mine alone.

133
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:51,770
This is a fine horse.

134
00:08:51,770 --> 00:08:52,630
It helped me greatly.

135
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,530
Mingke, he is praising you.

136
00:08:58,770 --> 00:08:59,970
It was all for Your Majesty.

137
00:09:00,130 --> 00:09:01,370
How could this servant claim credit?

138
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:03,770
Unlike Prince Yu, whose filial devotion

139
00:09:03,770 --> 00:09:05,930
led him to prepare such a fine steed for Your Majesty.

140
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,570
Indeed. Attendants.

141
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,200
Bring over the horse Prince Yu offered.

142
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:14,100
Yes.

143
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:26,600
This horse has a fierce temper.

144
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,730
Who has the skill to tame it?

145
00:09:30,130 --> 00:09:31,100
I am willing to try.

146
00:09:31,370 --> 00:09:32,370
Good. Go.

147
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:37,630
Good horse, good horse.

148
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,530
This time, please do me the honor.

149
00:09:45,070 --> 00:09:46,130
The horse has gone mad!

150
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:48,530
The horse has gone mad!

151
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:52,970
I cannot stop! Help!

152
00:09:58,700 --> 00:09:59,730
Protect His Majesty!

153
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:01,600
This is bad.

154
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:02,730
Something is wrong with that horse.

155
00:10:36,270 --> 00:10:37,300
Your Majesty, you were startled.

156
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:38,730
This servant arrived too late.

157
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:45,100
Chu Mingke.
